analysis tools. Currently, TSK supports several filesystems, as NTFS, FAT, exFAT, HFS+, Ext3, Ext4, UFS and YAFFS2. This package contains the set of command line tools in The Sleuth Kit.","features":["تحليل الأدلة الرقمية","استعادة الملفات","البيانات الوصفية"]},{"name":"srch_strings","cat":"forensics","sub":"Sleuth Kit Suite","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/sleuthkit/#srch_strings","cats":["forensics"],"status":"تحقيق جنائي","equiv":"","slug":"sleuthkit","version":"4.14.0+dfsg-0kali1","arch":"any all","homepage":"https://www.sleuthkit.org/sleuthkit","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/sleuthkit","summary":"Tools for forensics analysis on volume and filesystem data","desc":"The Sleuth Kit, also known as TSK, is a collection of UNIX-based command line file and volume system forensic analysis tools. The filesystem tools allow you to examine filesystems of a suspect computer in a non-intrusive fashion. Because the tools do not rely on the operating system to process the filesystems, deleted and hidden content is shown. The volume system (media management) tools allow you to examine the layout of disks and other media. You can also recover deleted files, get information stored in slack spaces, examine filesystems journal, see partitions layout on disks or images etc. But is very important clarify that the TSK acts over the current filesystem only. The Sleuth Kit supports DOS partitions, BSD partitions (disk labels), Mac partitions, Sun slices (Volume Table of Contents), and GPT disks. With these tools, you can identify where partitions are located and extract them so that they can be analyzed with filesystem analysis tools. Currently, TSK supports several filesystems, as NTFS, FAT, exFAT, HFS+, Ext3, Ext4, UFS and YAFFS2. This package contains the set of command line tools in The Sleuth Kit.","features":["تحليل الأدلة الرقمية","استعادة الملفات","البيانات الوصفية"]},{"name":"tsk_comparedir","cat":"forensics","sub":"Sleuth Kit Suite","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/sleuthkit/#tsk_comparedir","cats":["forensics"],"status":"تحقيق جنائي","equiv":"","slug":"sleuthkit","version":"4.14.0+dfsg-0kali1","arch":"any all","homepage":"https://www.sleuthkit.org/sleuthkit","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/sleuthkit","summary":"Tools for forensics analysis on volume and filesystem data","desc":"The Sleuth Kit, also known as TSK, is a collection of UNIX-based command line file and volume system forensic analysis tools. The filesystem tools allow you to examine filesystems of a suspect computer in a non-intrusive fashion. Because the tools do not rely on the operating system to process the filesystems, deleted and hidden content is shown. The volume system (media management) tools allow you to examine the layout of disks and other media. You can also recover deleted files, get information stored in slack spaces, examine filesystems journal, see partitions layout on disks or images etc. But is very important clarify that the TSK acts over the current filesystem only. The Sleuth Kit supports DOS partitions, BSD partitions (disk labels), Mac partitions, Sun slices (Volume Table of Contents), and GPT disks. With these tools, you can identify where partitions are located and extract them so that they can be analyzed with filesystem analysis tools. Currently, TSK supports several filesystems, as NTFS, FAT, exFAT, HFS+, Ext3, Ext4, UFS and YAFFS2. This package contains the set of command line tools in The Sleuth Kit.","features":["تحليل الأدلة الرقمية","استعادة الملفات","البيانات الوصفية"]},{"name":"tsk_gettimes","cat":"forensics","sub":"Sleuth Kit Suite","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/sleuthkit/#tsk_gettimes","cats":["forensics"],"status":"تحقيق جنائي","equiv":"","slug":"sleuthkit","version":"4.14.0+dfsg-0kali1","arch":"any all","homepage":"https://www.sleuthkit.org/sleuthkit","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/sleuthkit","summary":"Tools for forensics analysis on volume and filesystem data","desc":"The Sleuth Kit, also known as TSK, is a collection of UNIX-based command line file and volume system forensic analysis tools. The filesystem tools allow you to examine filesystems of a suspect computer in a non-intrusive fashion. Because the tools do not rely on the operating system to process the filesystems, deleted and hidden content is shown. The volume system (media management) tools allow you to examine the layout of disks and other media. You can also recover deleted files, get information stored in slack spaces, examine filesystems journal, see partitions layout on disks or images etc. But is very important clarify that the TSK acts over the current filesystem only. The Sleuth Kit supports DOS partitions, BSD partitions (disk labels), Mac partitions, Sun slices (Volume Table of Contents), and GPT disks. With these tools, you can identify where partitions are located and extract them so that they can be analyzed with filesystem analysis tools. Currently, TSK supports several filesystems, as NTFS, FAT, exFAT, HFS+, Ext3, Ext4, UFS and YAFFS2. This package contains the set of command line tools in The Sleuth Kit.","features":["تحليل الأدلة الرقمية","استعادة الملفات","البيانات الوصفية"]},{"name":"tsk_loaddb","cat":"forensics","sub":"Sleuth Kit Suite","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/sleuthkit/#tsk_loaddb","cats":["forensics"],"status":"تحقيق جنائي","equiv":"","slug":"sleuthkit","version":"4.14.0+dfsg-0kali1","arch":"any all","homepage":"https://www.sleuthkit.org/sleuthkit","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/sleuthkit","summary":"Tools for forensics analysis on volume and filesystem data","desc":"The Sleuth Kit, also known as TSK, is a collection of UNIX-based command line file and volume system forensic analysis tools. The filesystem tools allow you to examine filesystems of a suspect computer in a non-intrusive fashion. Because the tools do not rely on the operating system to process the filesystems, deleted and hidden content is shown. The volume system (media management) tools allow you to examine the layout of disks and other media. You can also recover deleted files, get information stored in slack spaces, examine filesystems journal, see partitions layout on disks or images etc. But is very important clarify that the TSK acts over the current filesystem only. The Sleuth Kit supports DOS partitions, BSD partitions (disk labels), Mac partitions, Sun slices (Volume Table of Contents), and GPT disks. With these tools, you can identify where partitions are located and extract them so that they can be analyzed with filesystem analysis tools. Currently, TSK supports several filesystems, as NTFS, FAT, exFAT, HFS+, Ext3, Ext4, UFS and YAFFS2. This package contains the set of command line tools in The Sleuth Kit.","features":["تحليل الأدلة الرقمية","استعادة الملفات","البيانات الوصفية"]},{"name":"tsk_recover","cat":"forensics","sub":"Sleuth Kit Suite","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/sleuthkit/#tsk_recover","cats":["forensics"],"status":"دفاعي","equiv":"","slug":"sleuthkit","version":"4.14.0+dfsg-0kali1","arch":"any all","homepage":"https://www.sleuthkit.org/sleuthkit","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/sleuthkit","summary":"Tools for forensics analysis on volume and filesystem data","desc":"The Sleuth Kit, also known as TSK, is a collection of UNIX-based command line file and volume system forensic analysis tools. The filesystem tools allow you to examine filesystems of a suspect computer in a non-intrusive fashion. Because the tools do not rely on the operating system to process the filesystems, deleted and hidden content is shown. The volume system (media management) tools allow you to examine the layout of disks and other media. You can also recover deleted files, get information stored in slack spaces, examine filesystems journal, see partitions layout on disks or images etc. But is very important clarify that the TSK acts over the current filesystem only. The Sleuth Kit supports DOS partitions, BSD partitions (disk labels), Mac partitions, Sun slices (Volume Table of Contents), and GPT disks. With these tools, you can identify where partitions are located and extract them so that they can be analyzed with filesystem analysis tools. Currently, TSK supports several filesystems, as NTFS, FAT, exFAT, HFS+, Ext3, Ext4, UFS and YAFFS2. This package contains the set of command line tools in The Sleuth Kit.","features":["تحليل الأدلة الرقمية","استعادة الملفات","البيانات الوصفية"]},{"name":"binwalk","cat":"forensics","sub":"Sleuth Kit Suite","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/binwalk/#binwalk-1","cats":["forensics"],"status":"دفاعي","equiv":"","slug":"binwalk","version":"2.4.3+dfsg1-3","arch":"all","homepage":"https://github.com/ReFirmLabs/binwalk","repo":"https://salsa.debian.org/pkg-security-team/binwalk","summary":"Tool library for analyzing binary blobs and executable code","desc":"Binwalk is a tool for searching a given binary image for embedded files and executable code. Specifically, it is designed for identifying files and code embedded inside of firmware images. Binwalk uses the libmagic library, so it is compatible with magic signatures created for the Unix file utility. Binwalk also includes a custom magic signature file which contains improved signatures for files that are commonly found in firmware images such as compressed/archived files, firmware headers, Linux kernels, bootloaders, filesystems, etc. This package is an empty package, because the binary tool is already provided with the library, dependency of this package.","features":["تحليل الأدلة الرقمية","استعادة الملفات","البيانات الوصفية"]},{"name":"binwalk3","cat":"forensics","sub":"Sleuth Kit Suite","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/binwalk3/#binwalk3-1","cats":["forensics"],"status":"تحقيق جنائي","equiv":"","slug":"binwalk3","version":"3.1.0-0kali4","arch":"arm64 amd64","homepage":"https://github.com/ReFirmLabs/binwalk","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/binwalk3","summary":"Tool library for analyzing binary blobs and executable code","desc":"Binwalk is a tool for identifying, and optionally extracting, files and data that have been embedded inside of other files. While its primary focus is firmware analysis, it supports a wide variety of file and data types. Through entropy analysis, it can even help to identify unknown compression or encryption! Binwalk can be customized and integrated into your own Rust projects This is an updated version of the Binwalk firmware analysis tool, re-written in Rust for speed and accuracy.","features":["تحليل الأدلة الرقمية","استعادة الملفات","البيانات الوصفية"]},{"name":"bulk_extractor","cat":"forensics","sub":"Sleuth Kit Suite","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/bulk-extractor/#bulk_extractor","cats":["forensics"],"status":"دفاعي","equiv":"","slug":"bulk-extractor","version":"2.1.1+git20260109.898db1-0kali3","arch":"amd64 arm64","homepage":"https://github.com/simsong/bulk_extractor","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/bulk-extractor","summary":"Extracts information without parsing filesystem","desc":"bulk_extractor is a C++ program that scans a disk image, a file, or a directory of files and extracts useful information without parsing the file system or file system structures. The results are stored in feature files that can be easily inspected, parsed, or processed with automated tools. bulk_extractor also creates histograms of features that it finds, as features that are more common tend to be more important.","features":["تحليل الأدلة الرقمية","استعادة الملفات","البيانات الوصفية"]},{"name":"chkrootkit","cat":"forensics","sub":"Sleuth Kit Suite","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/chkrootkit/#chkrootkit-1","cats":["forensics"],"status":"دفاعي","equiv":"","slug":"chkrootkit","version":"0.59-2","arch":"any","homepage":"https://www.chkrootkit.org/","repo":"https://salsa.debian.org/pkg-security-team/chkrootkit","summary":"Rootkit detector","desc":"The chkrootkit security scanner searches for signs that the system is infected with a 'rootkit'. Rootkits are a form of malware that seek to exploit security flaws to grant unauthorised access to a computer or its services, generally for malicious purposes. chkrootkit can identify signs of over 70 different rootkits (see the project's website for a list). Please note that an automated tool like chkrootkit can never guarantee a system is uncompromised. Nor does every report always signify a genuine problem: human judgement and further investigation will always be needed to assure the security of your system.","features":["تحليل الأدلة الرقمية","استعادة الملفات","البيانات الوصفية"]},{"name":"galleta","cat":"forensics","sub":"Sleuth Kit Suite","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/galleta/#galleta-1","cats":["forensics"],"status":"تحقيق جنائي","equiv":"","slug":"galleta","version":"1.0+20040505-12","arch":"any","homepage":"https://odessa.sourceforge.net/","repo":"https://salsa.debian.org/pkg-security-team/galleta","summary":"Internet Explorer cookie forensic analysis tool","desc":"Galleta is a forensics tool that examines the content of cookie files produced by Microsoft Internet Explorer (MSIE). It parses the file and outputs a field separated that can be loaded in a spreadsheet.","features":["تحليل الأدلة الرقمية","استعادة الملفات","البيانات الوصفية"]},{"name":"hashdeep","cat":"forensics","sub":"Sleuth Kit Suite","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/hashdeep/#hashdeep-1","cats":["forensics"],"status":"دفاعي","equiv":"","slug":"hashdeep","version":"4.4+git20170824+ds-1","arch":"any","homepage":"https://md5deep.sourceforge.net","repo":"https://salsa.debian.org/pkg-security-team/hashdeep","summary":"Recursively compute hashsums or piecewise hashings","desc":"hashdeep is a set of tools to compute MD5, SHA1, SHA256, tiger and whirlpool hashsums of arbitrary number of files recursively. The main hashdeep features are: does not match; sized blocks). This package is useful in forensics investigations.","features":["It can compare those hashsums with a list of known hashes;","The tools can display those that match the list or those that","It can display a time estimation when processing large files.","It can do piecewise hashing (hash input files in arbitrary"]},{"name":"rkhunter","cat":"forensics","sub":"Sleuth Kit Suite","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/rkhunter/#rkhunter-1","cats":["forensics"],"status":"دفاعي","equiv":"","slug":"rkhunter","version":"1.4.6-14","arch":"all","homepage":"https://rkhunter.sourceforge.net","repo":"https://salsa.debian.org/pkg-security-team/rkhunter","summary":"Rootkit, backdoor, sniffer and exploit scanner","desc":"Rootkit Hunter scans systems for known and unknown rootkits, backdoors, sniffers and exploits. It checks for: and can optionally scan within files. Using rkhunter alone does not guarantee that a system is not compromised. Running additional tests, such as chkrootkit, is recommended.","features":["SHA256 hash changes;","files commonly created by rootkits;","executables with anomalous file permissions;","suspicious strings in kernel modules;","hidden files in system directories;"]},{"name":"ssdeep","cat":"forensics","sub":"Sleuth Kit Suite","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/ssdeep/#ssdeep-1","cats":["forensics"],"status":"دفاعي","equiv":"","slug":"ssdeep","version":"2.14.1+git20180629.57fcfff-3","arch":"any","homepage":"https://github.com/ssdeep-project/ssdeep","repo":"https://salsa.debian.org/pkg-security-team/ssdeep","summary":"Recursive piecewise hashing tool","desc":"ssdeep is a tool for recursive computing and matching of Context Triggered Piecewise Hashing (aka Fuzzy Hashing). Fuzzy hashing is a method for comparing similar but not identical files. This tool can be used to compare files like regular hashing does (like md5sum or sha1sum) but it will find similar files with little differences. For example, it can be used to identify modified versions of known files even if data has been inserted, modified, or deleted in the new files. This package is useful in forensics investigations.","features":["تحليل الأدلة الرقمية","استعادة الملفات","البيانات الوصفية"]},{"name":"unhide","cat":"forensics","sub":"Sleuth Kit Suite","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/unhide/#unhide-1","cats":["forensics"],"status":"تحقيق جنائي","equiv":"","slug":"unhide","version":"20240510-2","arch":"any","homepage":"https://www.unhide-forensics.info","repo":"https://salsa.debian.org/pkg-security-team/unhide","summary":"Forensic tool to find hidden processes and ports","desc":"Unhide is a forensic tool to find processes and TCP/UDP ports hidden by rootkits, Linux kernel modules or by other techniques. It includes two utilities: unhide and unhide-tcp. unhide detects hidden processes using the following six techniques: procfs. (syscall scanning). kernel (/bin/ps output vs /proc, procfs walking and syscall) unhide-tcp identifies TCP/UDP ports that are listening but are not listed in /bin/netstat through brute forcing of all TCP/UDP ports available. This package can be used by rkhunter in its daily scans. This package is useful for network security checks, in addition to forensics investigations.","features":["Compare /proc vs /bin/ps output","Compare info gathered from /bin/ps with info gathered by walking thru the","Compare info gathered from /bin/ps with info gathered from syscalls","Full PIDs space occupation (PIDs bruteforcing)","Reverse search, verify that all thread seen by ps are also seen by the","Quick compare /proc, procfs walking and syscall vs /bin/ps output"]},{"name":"xplico-webui-start","cat":"forensics","sub":"Sleuth Kit Suite","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/xplico/#xplico-webui-start","cats":["forensics","services-and-other-tools"],"status":"تحقيق جنائي","equiv":"","slug":"xplico","version":"1.2.2-0kali7","arch":"amd64 i386","homepage":"https://www.xplico.org","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/xplico","summary":"Network Forensic Analysis Tool (NFAT)","desc":"The goal of Xplico is extract from an internet traffic capture the applications data contained. For example, from a pcap file Xplico extracts each email (POP, IMAP, and SMTP protocols), all HTTP contents, each VoIP call (SIP, MGCP, H323), FTP, TFTP, and so on. Xplico is not a network protocol analyzer.","features":["تحليل الأدلة الرقمية","استعادة الملفات","البيانات الوصفية"]},{"name":"yara","cat":"forensics","sub":"Sleuth Kit Suite","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/yara/#yara-1","cats":["forensics"],"status":"دفاعي","equiv":"","slug":"yara","version":"4.5.8-1","arch":"any all","homepage":"https://virustotal.github.io/yara/","repo":"https://salsa.debian.org/pkg-security-team/yara","summary":"Pattern matching swiss knife for malware researchers","desc":"YARA is a tool aimed at helping malware researchers to identify and classify malware samples. With YARA, it is possible to create descriptions of malware families based on textual or binary patterns contained in samples of those families. Each description consists of a set of strings and a Boolean expression which determines its logic. Complex and powerful rules can be created by using binary strings with wild-cards, case-insensitive text strings, special operators, regular expressions and many other features.","features":["تحليل الأدلة الرقمية","استعادة الملفات","البيانات الوصفية"]},{"name":"cherrytree","cat":"services-and-other-tools","sub":"Reporting Tools","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/cherrytree/#cherrytree-1","cats":["services-and-other-tools"],"status":"خدمة","equiv":"","slug":"cherrytree","version":"1.2.0+dfsg-1","arch":"any","homepage":"https://www.giuspen.net/cherrytree/","repo":"https://salsa.debian.org/debian/cherrytree","summary":"Hierarchical note taking application","desc":"CherryTree is a hierarchical note taking application, featuring rich text, syntax highlighting, images handling, hyperlinks, import/export with support for multiple formats, support for multiple languages, and more.","features":["خدمات مساندة","أدوات نظام","إدارة البيئة"]},{"name":"dradis-start","cat":"services-and-other-tools","sub":"Reporting Tools","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/dradis/#dradis-start","cats":["services-and-other-tools"],"status":"خدمة","equiv":"","slug":"dradis","version":"5.3.0-0kali1","arch":"amd64","homepage":"https://dradis.com/ce/","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/dradis","summary":"Collaboration tools for penetration testing","desc":"Dradis is a tool to help you simplify reporting and collaboration. Dradis is an open-source project released in 2007 that has been refined for over a decade by security professionals around the world.","features":["Spend more time testing and less time reporting","Ensure consistent quality across your assessments","Combine the output of your favorite scanners"]},{"name":"faraday-start","cat":"services-and-other-tools","sub":"Reporting Tools","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/python-faraday/#faraday-start","cats":["services-and-other-tools"],"status":"خدمة","equiv":"","slug":"python-faraday","version":"5.22.0-0kali1","arch":"all","homepage":"https://faradaysec.com","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/python-faraday","summary":"Collaborative Penetration Test IDE","desc":"Faraday introduces a new concept (IPE) Integrated Penetration-Test Environment a multiuser Penetration test IDE. Designed for distribution, indexation and analysis of the generated data during the process of a security audit. The main purpose of Faraday is to re-use the available tools in the community to take advantage of them in a multiuser way. This package is a transitional package. It can be remove safely.","features":["خدمات مساندة","أدوات نظام","إدارة البيئة"]},{"name":"obsidian","cat":"services-and-other-tools","sub":"Reporting Tools","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/obsidian/#obsidian-1","cats":["services-and-other-tools"],"status":"خدمة","equiv":"","slug":"obsidian","version":"1.7.7-0kali1","arch":"amd64 arm64","homepage":"https://obsidian.md/","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/obsidian","summary":"Private and flexible writing app that adapts to the way you think","desc":"Obsidian stores notes on your device, so you can access them quickly, even offline. With hundreds of plugins and themes, you can shape Obsidian to fit your way of thinking. Obsidian uses open, non-proprietary files, so you're never locked in, and can preserve your data for the long term.","features":["خدمات مساندة","أدوات نظام","إدارة البيئة"]},{"name":"pipal","cat":"services-and-other-tools","sub":"Reporting Tools","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/pipal/#pipal-1","cats":["services-and-other-tools"],"status":"خدمة","equiv":"","slug":"pipal","version":"3.4.0-0kali1","arch":"all","homepage":"https://www.digininja.org/projects/pipal.php","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/pipal","summary":"Statistical analysis on password dumps","desc":"All this tool does is to give you the stats and the information to help you analyse the passwords. The real work is done by you in interpreting the results.","features":["خدمات مساندة","أدوات نظام","إدارة البيئة"]},{"name":"recordmydesktop","cat":"services-and-other-tools","sub":"Reporting Tools","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/recordmydesktop/#recordmydesktop-1","cats":["services-and-other-tools"],"status":"خدمة","equiv":"","slug":"recordmydesktop","version":"0.4.0-2","arch":"any","homepage":"https://enselic.github.io/recordmydesktop/","repo":"https://salsa.debian.org/debian/recordmydesktop","summary":"Captures audio-video data of a Linux desktop session","desc":"The application produces an ogg-encapsulated theora-vorbis file. recordMyDesktop tries to be as unobstrusive as possible by proccessing only regions of the screen that have changed","features":["خدمات مساندة","أدوات نظام","إدارة البيئة"]},{"name":"redeye-start","cat":"services-and-other-tools","sub":"Reporting Tools","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/redeye/#redeye-start","cats":["services-and-other-tools"],"status":"خدمة","equiv":"","slug":"redeye","version":"0.0~git20230722.347f493-0kali5","arch":"all","homepage":"https://github.com/redeye-framework/Redeye","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/redeye","summary":"Tool to help you manage your data during a pentest operation","desc":"This package contains a tool intended to help you manage your data during a pentest operation in the most efficient and organized way.","features":["خدمات مساندة","أدوات نظام","إدارة البيئة"]},{"name":"cutycapt","cat":"services-and-other-tools","sub":"Reporting Tools","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/cutycapt/#cutycapt-1","cats":["services-and-other-tools"],"status":"خدمة","equiv":"","slug":"cutycapt","version":"0.0+20200623-1","arch":"any","homepage":"https://github.com/Crystalix007/CutyCapt","repo":"https://salsa.debian.org/debian/cutycapt","summary":"Utility to capture WebKit's rendering of a web page","desc":"CutyCapt is a small cross-platform command-line utility to capture WebKit's rendering of a web page into a variety of vector and bitmap formats, including SVG, PDF, PS, PNG, JPEG, TIFF, GIF, and BMP.","features":["خدمات مساندة","أدوات نظام","إدارة البيئة"]},{"name":"eyewitness","cat":"services-and-other-tools","sub":"Reporting Tools","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/eyewitness/#eyewitness-1","cats":["services-and-other-tools"],"status":"خدمة","equiv":"","slug":"eyewitness","version":"20230525.1+git20230720-0kali4","arch":"amd64 arm64 i386","homepage":"https://www.christophertruncer.com/eyewitness-triage-tool/","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/eyewitness","summary":"Rapid web application triage tool","desc":"EyeWitness is designed to take screenshots of websites, provide some server header info, and identify default credentials if possible. Inspiration came from Tim Tomes's PeepingTom Script. EyeWitness is designed to run on Kali Linux. It will auto detect the file you give it with the -f flag as either being a text file with URLs on each new line, nmap xml output, or nessus xml output. The -t (timeout) flag is completely optional, and lets you provice the max time to wait when trying to render and screenshot a web page. The --open flag, which is optional, will open the URL in a new tab within Firefox.","features":["خدمات مساندة","أدوات نظام","إدارة البيئة"]},{"name":"witnessme","cat":"services-and-other-tools","sub":"Reporting Tools","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/witnessme/#witnessme-1","cats":["services-and-other-tools"],"status":"خدمة","equiv":"","slug":"witnessme","version":"1.5.0+git20201026-0kali4","arch":"all","homepage":"https://github.com/byt3bl33d3r/WitnessMe","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/witnessme","summary":"Web Inventory tool","desc":"This package contains a Web Inventory tool inspired by Eyewitness, its also written to be extensible allowing you to create custom functionality that can take advantage of the headless browser it drives in the back-end.","features":["خدمات مساندة","أدوات نظام","إدارة البيئة"]},{"name":"juice-shop-start","cat":"services-and-other-tools","sub":"Reporting Tools","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/juice-shop/#juice-shop-start","cats":["services-and-other-tools"],"status":"خدمة","equiv":"","slug":"juice-shop","version":"19.1.1-0kali4","arch":"amd64","homepage":"https://github.com/juice-shop/juice-shop","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/juice-shop","summary":"Insecure web application","desc":"This package contains a modern and sophisticated insecure web application! It can be used in security trainings, awareness demos, CTFs and as a guinea pig for security tools! Juice Shop encompasses vulnerabilities from the entire OWASP Top Ten along with many other security flaws found in real-world applications! WARNING: Do not upload it to your hosting provider's public html folder or any Internet facing servers, as they will be compromised.","features":["خدمات مساندة","أدوات نظام","إدارة البيئة"]},{"name":"dvwa-start","cat":"services-and-other-tools","sub":"Reporting Tools","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/dvwa/#dvwa-start","cats":["services-and-other-tools"],"status":"خدمة","equiv":"","slug":"dvwa","version":"2.5-0kali1","arch":"all","homepage":"https://github.com/digininja/DVWA","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/dvwa","summary":"Damn Vulnerable Web Application","desc":"This package contains a PHP/MySQL web application that is damn vulnerable. Its main goal is to be an aid for security professionals to test their skills and tools in a legal environment, help web developers better understand the processes of securing web applications and to aid both students & teachers to learn about web application security in a controlled class room environment. The aim of DVWA is to practice some of the most common web vulnerabilities, with various levels of difficulty, with a simple straightforward interface. Please note, there are both documented and undocumented vulnerabilities with this software. This is intentional. You are encouraged to try and discover as many issues as possible. WARNING: Do not upload it to your hosting provider's public html folder or any Internet facing servers, as they will be compromised.","features":["خدمات مساندة","أدوات نظام","إدارة البيئة"]},{"name":"beef-xss-stop","cat":"services-and-other-tools","sub":"System Services","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/beef-xss/#beef-xss-stop","cats":["services-and-other-tools"],"status":"خدمة","equiv":"","slug":"beef-xss","version":"0.6.0.0-0kali6","arch":"any","homepage":"https://beefproject.com/","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/beef-xss","summary":"Browser Exploitation Framework (BeEF)","desc":"BeEF is short for The Browser Exploitation Framework. It is a penetration testing tool that focuses on the web browser. Amid growing concerns about web-born attacks against clients, including mobile clients, BeEF allows the professional penetration tester to assess the actual security posture of a target environment by using client-side attack vectors. Unlike other security frameworks, BeEF looks past the hardened network perimeter and client system, and examines exploitability within the context of the one open door: the web browser. BeEF will hook one or more web browsers and use them as beachheads for launching directed command modules and further attacks against the system from within the browser context.","features":["خدمات مساندة","أدوات نظام","إدارة البيئة"]},{"name":"defectdojo-start","cat":"services-and-other-tools","sub":"System Services","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/defectdojo/#defectdojo-start","cats":["services-and-other-tools"],"status":"خدمة","equiv":"","slug":"defectdojo","version":"2.37.3-0kali7","arch":"amd64 arm64 armhf","homepage":"https://github.com/DefectDojo/django-DefectDojo","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/defectdojo","summary":"Security orchestration and vulnerability management platform","desc":"This package contains a security orchestration and vulnerability management platform. DefectDojo allows you to manage your application security program, maintain product and application information, triage vulnerabilities and push findings to systems like JIRA and Slack. DefectDojo enriches and refines vulnerability data using a number of heuristic algorithms that improve with the more you use the platform.","features":["خدمات مساندة","أدوات نظام","إدارة البيئة"]},{"name":"defectdojo-stop","cat":"services-and-other-tools","sub":"System Services","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/defectdojo/#defectdojo-stop","cats":["services-and-other-tools"],"status":"خدمة","equiv":"","slug":"defectdojo","version":"2.37.3-0kali7","arch":"amd64 arm64 armhf","homepage":"https://github.com/DefectDojo/django-DefectDojo","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/defectdojo","summary":"Security orchestration and vulnerability management platform","desc":"This package contains a security orchestration and vulnerability management platform. DefectDojo allows you to manage your application security program, maintain product and application information, triage vulnerabilities and push findings to systems like JIRA and Slack. DefectDojo enriches and refines vulnerability data using a number of heuristic algorithms that improve with the more you use the platform.","features":["خدمات مساندة","أدوات نظام","إدارة البيئة"]},{"name":"dradis-stop","cat":"services-and-other-tools","sub":"System Services","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/dradis/#dradis-stop","cats":["services-and-other-tools"],"status":"خدمة","equiv":"","slug":"dradis","version":"5.3.0-0kali1","arch":"amd64","homepage":"https://dradis.com/ce/","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/dradis","summary":"Collaboration tools for penetration testing","desc":"Dradis is a tool to help you simplify reporting and collaboration. Dradis is an open-source project released in 2007 that has been refined for over a decade by security professionals around the world.","features":["Spend more time testing and less time reporting","Ensure consistent quality across your assessments","Combine the output of your favorite scanners"]},{"name":"dvwa-stop","cat":"services-and-other-tools","sub":"System Services","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/dvwa/#dvwa-stop","cats":["services-and-other-tools"],"status":"خدمة","equiv":"","slug":"dvwa","version":"2.5-0kali1","arch":"all","homepage":"https://github.com/digininja/DVWA","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/dvwa","summary":"Damn Vulnerable Web Application","desc":"This package contains a PHP/MySQL web application that is damn vulnerable. Its main goal is to be an aid for security professionals to test their skills and tools in a legal environment, help web developers better understand the processes of securing web applications and to aid both students & teachers to learn about web application security in a controlled class room environment. The aim of DVWA is to practice some of the most common web vulnerabilities, with various levels of difficulty, with a simple straightforward interface. Please note, there are both documented and undocumented vulnerabilities with this software. This is intentional. You are encouraged to try and discover as many issues as possible. WARNING: Do not upload it to your hosting provider's public html folder or any Internet facing servers, as they will be compromised.","features":["خدمات مساندة","أدوات نظام","إدارة البيئة"]},{"name":"faraday-stop","cat":"services-and-other-tools","sub":"System Services","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/python-faraday/#faraday-stop","cats":["services-and-other-tools"],"status":"خدمة","equiv":"","slug":"python-faraday","version":"5.22.0-0kali1","arch":"all","homepage":"https://faradaysec.com","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/python-faraday","summary":"Collaborative Penetration Test IDE","desc":"Faraday introduces a new concept (IPE) Integrated Penetration-Test Environment a multiuser Penetration test IDE. Designed for distribution, indexation and analysis of the generated data during the process of a security audit. The main purpose of Faraday is to re-use the available tools in the community to take advantage of them in a multiuser way. This package is a transitional package. It can be remove safely.","features":["خدمات مساندة","أدوات نظام","إدارة البيئة"]},{"name":"gophish-stop","cat":"services-and-other-tools","sub":"System Services","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/gophish/#gophish-stop","cats":["services-and-other-tools"],"status":"خدمة","equiv":"","slug":"gophish","version":"0.12.1-0kali6","arch":"any","homepage":"https://getgophish.com/","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/gophish","summary":"Open-Source Phishing Toolkit","desc":"This package contains an open-source phishing toolkit designed for businesses and penetration testers. It provides the ability to quickly and easily setup and execute phishing engagements and security awareness training.","features":["خدمات مساندة","أدوات نظام","إدارة البيئة"]},{"name":"gvm-check-setup","cat":"services-and-other-tools","sub":"System Services","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/gvm/#gvm-check-setup","cats":["services-and-other-tools"],"status":"خدمة","equiv":"","slug":"gvm","version":"25.04.3","arch":"all","homepage":"https://www.greenbone.net/","repo":"https://salsa.debian.org/pkg-security-team/gvm","summary":"Remote network security auditor - metapackage and useful scripts","desc":"The Greenbone Vulnerability Manager is a modular security auditing tool, used for testing remote systems for vulnerabilities that should be fixed. This package installs all the required packages. It provides scripts to setup, start and stop the GVM services. The tool was previously named OpenVAS.","features":["خدمات مساندة","أدوات نظام","إدارة البيئة"]},{"name":"gvm-setup","cat":"services-and-other-tools","sub":"System Services","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/gvm/#gvm-setup","cats":["services-and-other-tools"],"status":"خدمة","equiv":"","slug":"gvm","version":"25.04.3","arch":"all","homepage":"https://www.greenbone.net/","repo":"https://salsa.debian.org/pkg-security-team/gvm","summary":"Remote network security auditor - metapackage and useful scripts","desc":"The Greenbone Vulnerability Manager is a modular security auditing tool, used for testing remote systems for vulnerabilities that should be fixed. This package installs all the required packages. It provides scripts to setup, start and stop the GVM services. The tool was previously named OpenVAS.","features":["خدمات مساندة","أدوات نظام","إدارة البيئة"]},{"name":"gvm-stop","cat":"services-and-other-tools","sub":"System Services","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/gvm/#gvm-stop","cats":["services-and-other-tools"],"status":"خدمة","equiv":"","slug":"gvm","version":"25.04.3","arch":"all","homepage":"https://www.greenbone.net/","repo":"https://salsa.debian.org/pkg-security-team/gvm","summary":"Remote network security auditor - metapackage and useful scripts","desc":"The Greenbone Vulnerability Manager is a modular security auditing tool, used for testing remote systems for vulnerabilities that should be fixed. This package installs all the required packages. It provides scripts to setup, start and stop the GVM services. The tool was previously named OpenVAS.","features":["خدمات مساندة","أدوات نظام","إدارة البيئة"]},{"name":"juice-shop-stop","cat":"services-and-other-tools","sub":"System Services","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/juice-shop/#juice-shop-stop","cats":["services-and-other-tools"],"status":"خدمة","equiv":"","slug":"juice-shop","version":"19.1.1-0kali4","arch":"amd64","homepage":"https://github.com/juice-shop/juice-shop","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/juice-shop","summary":"Insecure web application","desc":"This package contains a modern and sophisticated insecure web application! It can be used in security trainings, awareness demos, CTFs and as a guinea pig for security tools! Juice Shop encompasses vulnerabilities from the entire OWASP Top Ten along with many other security flaws found in real-world applications! WARNING: Do not upload it to your hosting provider's public html folder or any Internet facing servers, as they will be compromised.","features":["خدمات مساندة","أدوات نظام","إدارة البيئة"]},{"name":"portspoof-start","cat":"services-and-other-tools","sub":"System Services","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/portspoof/#portspoof-start","cats":["services-and-other-tools"],"status":"خدمة","equiv":"","slug":"portspoof","version":"1.4-0kali2","arch":"any","homepage":"https://github.com/drk1wi/portspoof","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/portspoof","summary":"Enhance OS security through a set of techniques","desc":"This package contains a service to enhance OS security through a set of following techniques: Instead of informing an attacker that a particular port is in a CLOSED or FILTERED state Portspoof will return SYN+ACK for every port connection attempt/ Portspoof has a huge database of dynamic service signatures, that will be used to generate fake banners and fool scanners. This tool requires configuration before use.","features":["All 65535 TCP ports are always open","Every open TCP port emulates a service"]},{"name":"portspoof-stop","cat":"services-and-other-tools","sub":"System Services","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/portspoof/#portspoof-stop","cats":["services-and-other-tools"],"status":"خدمة","equiv":"","slug":"portspoof","version":"1.4-0kali2","arch":"any","homepage":"https://github.com/drk1wi/portspoof","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/portspoof","summary":"Enhance OS security through a set of techniques","desc":"This package contains a service to enhance OS security through a set of following techniques: Instead of informing an attacker that a particular port is in a CLOSED or FILTERED state Portspoof will return SYN+ACK for every port connection attempt/ Portspoof has a huge database of dynamic service signatures, that will be used to generate fake banners and fool scanners. This tool requires configuration before use.","features":["All 65535 TCP ports are always open","Every open TCP port emulates a service"]},{"name":"redeye-stop","cat":"services-and-other-tools","sub":"System Services","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/redeye/#redeye-stop","cats":["services-and-other-tools"],"status":"خدمة","equiv":"","slug":"redeye","version":"0.0~git20230722.347f493-0kali5","arch":"all","homepage":"https://github.com/redeye-framework/Redeye","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/redeye","summary":"Tool to help you manage your data during a pentest operation","desc":"This package contains a tool intended to help you manage your data during a pentest operation in the most efficient and organized way.","features":["خدمات مساندة","أدوات نظام","إدارة البيئة"]},{"name":"starkiller-stop","cat":"services-and-other-tools","sub":"System Services","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/powershell-empire/#starkiller-stop","cats":["services-and-other-tools"],"status":"خدمة","equiv":"","slug":"powershell-empire","version":"6.6.0-0kali1","arch":"all","homepage":"https://github.com/BC-SECURITY/Empire","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/powershell-empire","summary":"PowerShell and Python post-exploitation agent","desc":"This package contains a post-exploitation framework that includes a pure-PowerShell2.0 Windows agent, and a pure Python Linux/OS X agent. It is the merge of the previous PowerShell Empire and Python EmPyre projects. The framework offers cryptologically-secure communications and a flexible architecture. On the PowerShell side, Empire implements the ability to run PowerShell agents without needing powershell.exe, rapidly deployable post-exploitation modules ranging from key loggers to Mimikatz, and adaptable communications to evade network detection, all wrapped up in a usability-focused framework.","features":["خدمات مساندة","أدوات نظام","إدارة البيئة"]},{"name":"xplico-webui-stop","cat":"services-and-other-tools","sub":"System Services","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/xplico/#xplico-webui-stop","cats":["services-and-other-tools"],"status":"خدمة","equiv":"","slug":"xplico","version":"1.2.2-0kali7","arch":"amd64 i386","homepage":"https://www.xplico.org","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/xplico","summary":"Network Forensic Analysis Tool (NFAT)","desc":"The goal of Xplico is extract from an internet traffic capture the applications data contained. For example, from a pcap file Xplico extracts each email (POP, IMAP, and SMTP protocols), all HTTP contents, each VoIP call (SIP, MGCP, H323), FTP, TFTP, and so on. Xplico is not a network protocol analyzer.","features":["خدمات مساندة","أدوات نظام","إدارة البيئة"]},{"name":"arsenal-ng","cat":"services-and-other-tools","sub":"System Services","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/arsenal-ng/#arsenal-ng-1","cats":["services-and-other-tools"],"status":"خدمة","equiv":"","slug":"arsenal-ng","version":"1.6-0kali1","arch":"any","homepage":"https://github.com/halilkirazkaya/arsenal-ng","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/arsenal-ng","summary":"Go-based command library equipped with 200+ cybersecurity cheat-sheets","desc":"Inspired by arsenal, rewritten from scratch with a focus on simplicity, speed and developer experience. The classic launcher, evolved. Fast, Go-based command library equipped with 200+ cybersecurity cheat-sheets. Just install and start hacking.","features":["خدمات مساندة","أدوات نظام","إدارة البيئة"]},{"name":"gemini-cli","cat":"services-and-other-tools","sub":"System Services","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/gemini-cli/#gemini-cli-1","cats":["services-and-other-tools"],"status":"خدمة","equiv":"","slug":"gemini-cli","version":"0.58.0-0kali1","arch":"all","homepage":"https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/gemini-cli","summary":"Open-source AI agent","desc":"This package contains an open-source AI agent that brings the power of Gemini directly into your terminal. It provides lightweight access to Gemini, giving you the most direct path from your prompt to the model.","features":["خدمات مساندة","أدوات نظام","إدارة البيئة"]},{"name":"hexstrike_server","cat":"services-and-other-tools","sub":"System Services","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/hexstrike-ai/#hexstrike_server","cats":["services-and-other-tools"],"status":"خدمة","equiv":"","slug":"hexstrike-ai","version":"0.0~git20260803.d689933-0kali1","arch":"all","homepage":"https://github.com/0x4m4/hexstrike-ai","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/hexstrike-ai","summary":"AI-Powered MCP Cybersecurity Automation Platform","desc":"This package contains an HexStrike AI MCP v6.0 which features a multi-agent architecture with autonomous AI agents, intelligent decision-making, and vulnerability intelligence.","features":["خدمات مساندة","أدوات نظام","إدارة البيئة"]},{"name":"kali-tweaks","cat":"services-and-other-tools","sub":"System Services","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/kali-tweaks/#kali-tweaks-1","cats":["services-and-other-tools"],"status":"خدمة","equiv":"","slug":"kali-tweaks","version":"2026.2.0","arch":"all","homepage":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/kali-tweaks","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/kali-tweaks","summary":"Tool to adjust advanced configuration settings for Kali Linux","desc":"This package provides tweaks for Kali Linux. This include things like:","features":["Shell configuration","APT mirrors configuration","Kali Linux metapackages installation and removal","Hardening of the system","Additional configuration for virtualized environments","Kernel settings"]},{"name":"pwsh","cat":"services-and-other-tools","sub":"System Services","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/powershell/#pwsh-1","cats":["services-and-other-tools"],"status":"خدمة","equiv":"","slug":"powershell","version":"7.6.6-1.deb","arch":"amd64","homepage":"https://microsoft.com/powershell","repo":"","summary":"PowerShell is an automation and configuration management platform.","desc":"It consists of a cross-platform command-line shell and associated scripting language.","features":["خدمات مساندة","أدوات نظام","إدارة البيئة"]},{"name":"shell-gpt","cat":"services-and-other-tools","sub":"System Services","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/shell-gpt/#shell-gpt","cats":["services-and-other-tools"],"status":"خدمة","equiv":"","slug":"shell-gpt","version":"1.5.1-0kali1","arch":"all","homepage":"https://github.com/TheR1D/shell_gpt","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/shell-gpt","summary":"Command-line productivity tool powered by AI large language models","desc":"A command-line productivity tool powered by AI large language models (LLM). This command-line tool offers streamlined generation of shell commands, code snippets, documentation, eliminating the need for external resources (like Google search). Supports Linux, macOS, Windows and compatible with all major Shells like PowerShell, CMD, Bash, Zsh, etc.","features":["خدمات مساندة","أدوات نظام","إدارة البيئة"]},{"name":"tailscale","cat":"services-and-other-tools","sub":"System Services","url":"https://www.kali.org/tools/tailscale/#tailscale-1","cats":["services-and-other-tools"],"status":"خدمة","equiv":"","slug":"tailscale","version":"1.94.1-0kali4","arch":"any","homepage":"https://github.com/tailscale/tailscale","repo":"https://gitlab.com/kalilinux/packages/tailscale","summary":"Secure connectivity platform","desc":"This package contains the tailscaled daemon and the tailscale CLI tool. The tailscaled daemon runs on Linux.","features":["خدمات مساندة","أدوات نظام","إدارة البيئة"]}]}''')
CATEGORIES = _DATA["categories"]
TOOLS = _DATA["tools"]
CATEGORY_NAMES = {item["id"]: item["ar"] for item in CATEGORIES}
CATEGORY_EN = {item["id"]: item["en"] for item in CATEGORIES}
CATEGORY_OPTIONS = [["all", "كل التصنيفات"]] + [[item["id"], item["ar"] + " (%d)" % item["count"]] for item in CATEGORIES]
STATUS_OPTIONS = [
    ["all", "كل الحالات"],
    ["safe", "دفاعي وتحقيق جنائي"],
    ["recon", "استطلاع — مصرّح فقط"],
    ["offensive", "هجومي — مرجع فقط"],
    ["other", "خدمات وتطوير وعتاد"],
]
SHOW_LIMIT = 80


class KaliArsenalIndex(BasePlugin):
    def __init__(self):
        super().__init__()
        self.query = ""
        self.category = "all"
        self.status = "all"
        self.limit = SHOW_LIMIT
        self.selected = ""
        self.notice = ""

    def on_plugin_load(self):
        self.add_module(
            "Kali Arsenal Index",
            "فهرس رسمي لأدوات كالي: 501 أداة مع الوصف والخصائص وبيانات الحزمة",
            "rounded:terminal",
            "main",
            "PLUGINS",
            160,
        )

    def _reset_limit(self):
        self.limit = SHOW_LIMIT

    def _set_query(self, value):
        self.query = str(value or "")
        self._reset_limit()
        self.refresh()

    def _set_category(self, value):
        self.category = str(value or "all")
        self._reset_limit()
        self.refresh()

    def _set_status(self, value):
        self.status = str(value or "all")
        self._reset_limit()
        self.refresh()

    def _show_more(self):
        self.limit += SHOW_LIMIT
        self.refresh()

    def _status_bucket(self, status):
        if status.startswith("هجومي"):
            return "offensive"
        if status.startswith("استطلاع"):
            return "recon"
        if status.startswith("دفاعي") or status.startswith("تحقيق"):
            return "safe"
        return "other"

    def _filtered(self):
        query = self.query.strip().lower()
        result = []
        for tool in TOOLS:
            if self.category != "all" and self.category not in tool["cats"]:
                continue
            if self.status != "all" and self._status_bucket(tool["status"]) != self.status:
                continue
            haystack = " ".join(
                [
                    tool["name"],
                    tool["sub"],
                    tool.get("summary", ""),
                    tool.get("desc", ""),
                    tool.get("version", ""),
                    tool.get("slug", ""),
                    " ".join(tool.get("features", [])),
                ]
                + [CATEGORY_NAMES.get(cid, cid) + " " + CATEGORY_EN.get(cid, cid) for cid in tool["cats"]]
            ).lower()
            if query and query not in haystack:
                continue
            result.append(tool)
        return result

    def _find(self, name):
        for tool in TOOLS:
            if tool["name"] == name:
                return tool
        return None

    def _open_tool(self, name):
        self.selected = str(name)
        self.notice = ""
        self.navigate("detail")
        self.refresh()

    def _tool_callback(self, name):
        def callback(value=None):
            self._open_tool(name)

        return callback

    def _open_url(self, url, success):
        if not url:
            self.notice = "لا يوجد رابط رسمي متاح لهذه الأداة"
            self.refresh()
            return
        try:
            opened = bool(self.api.getAndroid().openUrl(url))
        except Exception as error:
            opened = False
            self.notice = "تعذر فتح الرابط: " + str(error)
        if opened:
            self.notice = success
        elif not self.notice:
            self.notice = "لا يوجد تطبيق متصفح لفتح الرابط"
        self.refresh()

    def _open_docs(self):
        tool = self._find(self.selected)
        if tool:
            self._open_url(tool["url"], "تم فتح الوثائق الرسمية")

    def _open_homepage(self):
        tool = self._find(self.selected)
        if tool:
            self._open_url(tool.get("homepage", ""), "تم فتح الموقع الرسمي")

    def _open_repo(self):
        tool = self._find(self.selected)
        if tool:
            self._open_url(tool.get("repo", ""), "تم فتح مستودع الحزمة")

    def _copy_text(self, text, success):
        try:
            self.api.getAndroid().clipboardSet(text)
            self.notice = success
        except Exception as error:
            self.notice = "تعذر النسخ: " + str(error)
        self.refresh()

    def _copy_tool(self):
        tool = self._find(self.selected)
        if tool:
            self._copy_text(tool["name"] + " — " + tool["url"], "تم نسخ الاسم والرابط")

    def _copy_details(self):
        tool = self._find(self.selected)
        if not tool:
            return
        parts = [
            tool["name"],
            tool.get("summary", ""),
            "الإصدار: " + (tool.get("version") or "غير متوفر"),
            "المعمارية: " + (tool.get("arch") or "غير متوفر"),
            "التصنيف: " + self._category_text(tool),
            "الحالة: " + tool["status"],
            "الوثائق: " + tool["url"],
        ]
        if tool.get("homepage"):
            parts.append("الموقع: " + tool["homepage"])
        self._copy_text("\n".join(parts), "تم نسخ بطاقة الأداة كاملة")

    def _open_source(self):
        self._open_url(_DATA["source"], "تم فتح مصدر كالي الرسمي")

    def _back(self):
        self.notice = ""
        self.navigate("main")
        self.refresh()

    def _status_color(self, status):
        if status.startswith("هجومي"):
            return "error"
        if status.startswith("دفاعي") or status.startswith("تحقيق"):
            return "primary"
        return None

    def _category_text(self, tool):
        names = [CATEGORY_NAMES.get(cid, cid) for cid in tool["cats"]]
        return "، ".join(names)

    def _subtitle(self, tool):
        summary = tool.get("summary") or tool["sub"]
        return self._category_text(tool) + " · " + summary + " · " + tool["status"]

    def _features_card(self, ui, tool):
        features = tool.get("features") or []
        nodes = [ui.text("الخصائص", "titleMedium")]
        if features:
            nodes.append(
                ui.text(
                    "خصائص موثقة من وصف حزمة كالي الرسمي. لا تتضمن أوامر تشغيل أو خطوات استغلال.",
                    "bodySmall",
                )
            )
            for item in features:
                nodes.append(ui.text("• " + item, "bodySmall"))
        else:
            nodes.append(ui.text("لا توجد قائمة خصائص مفصلة في صفحة الحزمة؛ راجع الوصف والوثائق الرسمية.", "bodySmall"))
        return ui.card(nodes)

    def screen_main(self, ui, api, state):
        matches = self._filtered()
        shown = matches[:self.limit]
        rows = []
        for tool in shown:
            rows.append(
                ui.function_row(
                    tool["name"],
                    self._subtitle(tool),
                    "terminal",
                    icon_tint=self._status_color(tool["status"]),
                    on_click=self._tool_callback(tool["name"]),
                )
            )
        nodes = [
            ui.card(
                [
                    ui.row(
                        [
                            ui.icon("terminal", 36),
                            ui.column(
                                [
                                    ui.text("Kali Arsenal Index", "titleLarge"),
                                    ui.text("فهرس رسمي بأوصاف وخصائص الأدوات — مرجع فقط", "bodySmall"),
                                ],
                                spacing=2,
                            ),
                        ],
                        spacing=12,
                    ),
                    ui.row(
                        [
                            ui.chip("%d أداة" % len(TOOLS), True),
                            ui.chip("%d تصنيفًا" % len(CATEGORIES), False),
                            ui.chip("%d خاصية" % sum(len(tool.get("features", [])) for tool in TOOLS), False),
                        ],
                        spacing=6,
                    ),
                    ui.text(
                        "كل أداة تعرض وصفها الرسمي وخصائصها وإصدارها ومعماريتها وموقعها ووثائقها. "
                        "الأدوات الهجومية مرجع فقط ولا ينفذها Dolphy.",
                        "bodySmall",
                    ),
                ]
            ),
            ui.card(
                [
                    ui.text("بحث وتصفية", "titleMedium"),
                    ui.text_field(self.query, self._set_query, "ابحث بالاسم أو الوصف أو الخاصية"),
                    ui.dropdown(CATEGORY_OPTIONS, self.category, self._set_category, "تصنيف كالي"),
                    ui.dropdown(STATUS_OPTIONS, self.status, self._set_status, "حالة التشغيل"),
                    ui.text(
                        "النتائج: %d — يُعرض %d" % (len(matches), len(shown)),
                        "bodySmall",
                    ),
                ]
            ),
        ]
        if rows:
            nodes.append(ui.segmented_list(rows))
        else:
            nodes.append(ui.card([ui.text("لا توجد أدوات مطابقة. جرّب اسمًا آخر أو تصنيفًا مختلفًا.", "bodySmall")]))
        if len(matches) > self.limit:
            nodes.append(
                ui.button(
                    "عرض المزيد (%d متبقية)" % (len(matches) - self.limit),
                    self._show_more,
                    style="tonal",
                    fill_max_width=True,
                )
            )
        nodes.extend(
            [
                ui.card(
                    [
                        ui.text("حدود الاستخدام", "titleMedium"),
                        ui.text(
                            "الفهرس لا يشغّل أي أداة هجومية ولا يقدّم أوامر أو تعليمات استغلال أو اعتراض. "
                            "أدوات الاستطلاع مسموحة فقط على شبكات وأجهزة تملك إذنًا صريحًا بفحصها.",
                            "bodySmall",
                        ),
                    ]
                ),
                ui.row(
                    [
                        ui.button("عن الفهرس", lambda value=None: (self.navigate("about"), self.refresh()), style="tonal", fill_max_width=True),
                        ui.button("فتح مصدر كالي", self._open_source, style="outlined", fill_max_width=True),
                    ],
                    spacing=8,
                ),
                ui.text("المصدر: " + _DATA["source"] + " · تحديث " + _DATA["updated"], "bodySmall"),
                ui.text(self.notice, "bodySmall", color="primary"),
            ]
        )
        return ui.scaffold(
            title="Kali Arsenal Index",
            content=ui.lazy_column(nodes, padding=16, spacing=12, fill_max_size=True),
        )

    def screen_detail(self, ui, api, state):
        tool = self._find(self.selected)
        if not tool:
            return self.screen_main(ui, api, state)
        nodes = [
            ui.card(
                [
                    ui.row(
                        [
                            ui.icon("terminal", 36, tint=self._status_color(tool["status"])),
                            ui.column(
                                [
                                    ui.text(tool["name"], "titleLarge"),
                                    ui.text(self._category_text(tool), "bodySmall"),
                                ],
                                spacing=2,
                            ),
                        ],
                        spacing=12,
                    ),
                    ui.row(
                        [
                            ui.chip(tool["status"], True),
                            ui.chip(tool["sub"], False),
                        ],
                        spacing=6,
                    ),
                    ui.text(tool.get("summary") or "أداة كالي رسمية", "titleSmall"),
                ]
            ),
            ui.card(
                [
                    ui.text("الوصف الرسمي", "titleMedium"),
                    ui.text(
                        tool.get("desc") or "لا يوجد وصف تفصيلي في صفحة الحزمة الرسمية؛ افتح الوثائق للتفاصيل.",
                        "bodySmall",
                    ),
                ]
            ),
            self._features_card(ui, tool),
            ui.card(
                [
                    ui.text("بيانات الحزمة", "titleMedium"),
                    ui.settings_row("الإصدار", tool.get("version") or "غير متوفر", "info"),
                    ui.settings_row("المعمارية", tool.get("arch") or "غير متوفر", "memory"),
                    ui.settings_row("اسم الحزمة", tool.get("slug") or tool["name"], "package"),
                    ui.settings_row("التصنيف الفرعي", tool["sub"], "label"),
                    ui.settings_row("الحالة", tool["status"], "info"),
                ]
            ),
        ]
        if tool["status"].startswith("هجومي"):
            nodes.append(
                ui.card(
                    [
                        ui.text("غير قابلة للتشغيل", "titleMedium", color="error"),
                        ui.text(
                            "هذه الأداة هجومية. لا يشغّلها Dolphy ولا يوفّر أوامر أو تعليمات استخدام أو استغلال. "
                            "الوصف والخصائص المعروضة مرجعية من الحزمة الرسمية فقط.",
                            "bodySmall",
                        ),
                    ]
                )
            )
        elif tool["status"].startswith("استطلاع"):
            nodes.append(
                ui.card(
                    [
                        ui.text("استخدام مصرّح فقط", "titleMedium", color="primary"),
                        ui.text(
                            "أداة استطلاع نشطة. استخدمها فقط على شبكة أو جهاز تملك إذنًا صريحًا بفحصه. "
                            "الفحص غير المصرّح قد يكون مخالفًا للقانون.",
                            "bodySmall",
                        ),
                    ]
                )
            )
        if tool.get("equiv"):
            nodes.append(
                ui.card(
                    [
                        ui.text("بديل دفاعي في Dolphy", "titleMedium", color="primary"),
                        ui.text(tool["equiv"], "bodySmall"),
                    ]
                )
            )
        if tool.get("homepage"):
            nodes.append(ui.button("فتح الموقع الرسمي", self._open_homepage, style="tonal", fill_max_width=True))
        if tool.get("repo"):
            nodes.append(ui.button("فتح مستودع الحزمة", self._open_repo, style="outlined", fill_max_width=True))
        nodes.extend(
            [
                ui.button("فتح الوثائق الرسمية", self._open_docs, fill_max_width=True),
                ui.button("نسخ بطاقة الأداة", self._copy_details, style="tonal", fill_max_width=True),
                ui.button("نسخ الاسم والرابط", self._copy_tool, style="text", fill_max_width=True),
                ui.button("رجوع إلى الفهرس", self._back, style="text", fill_max_width=True),
                ui.text(tool["url"], "bodySmall"),
                ui.text(self.notice, "bodySmall", color="primary"),
            ]
        )
        return ui.scaffold(
            title=tool["name"],
            content=ui.lazy_column(nodes, padding=16, spacing=12, fill_max_size=True),
        )

    def screen_about(self, ui, api, state):
        category_rows = []
        for item in CATEGORIES:
            category_rows.append(
                ui.settings_row(item["ar"], "%d أداة" % item["count"], "category")
            )
        return ui.scaffold(
            title="عن الفهرس",
            content=ui.lazy_column(
                [
                    ui.card(
                        [
                            ui.text("ما هذا الفهرس؟", "titleLarge"),
                            ui.text(
                                "فهرس رسمي لأدوات Kali Linux: %d أداة فريدة في %d تصنيفًا. "
                                "يجمع الاسم والوصف الرسمي والخصائص والإصدار والمعمارية والموقع والوثائق وحالة التشغيل."
                                % (len(TOOLS), len(CATEGORIES)),
                                "bodySmall",
                            ),
                            ui.text(
                                "الوصف والخصائص مأخوذان من مستودع توثيق كالي الرسمي، مع استبعاد أوامر التشغيل. "
                                "لا يحتوي الفهرس على تنفيذ للأدوات الهجومية أو تعليمات استغلال أو اعتراض أو كسر كلمات مرور.",
                                "bodySmall",
                            ),
                        ]
                    ),
                    ui.card(
                        [
                            ui.text("التصنيفات", "titleMedium"),
                            ui.segmented_list(category_rows),
                        ]
                    ),
                    ui.card(
                        [
                            ui.text("الأدوات الدفاعية", "titleMedium"),
                            ui.text(
                                "الأدوات الدفاعية العملية متاحة في Captive Portal Auditor: استطلاع Wi-Fi، كشف AP مزيّف، TLS، بصمة الويب، المنافذ، DNS، والتجزئة.",
                                "bodySmall",
                            ),
                        ]
                    ),
                    ui.button("فتح مصدر كالي الرسمي", self._open_source, fill_max_width=True),
                    ui.button("رجوع", self._back, style="text", fill_max_width=True),
                    ui.text(self.notice, "bodySmall", color="primary"),
                ],
                padding=16,
                spacing=12,
                fill_max_size=True,
            ),
        )
